T12 parent integration proposal (apply only in the parent integration checkout)

T12's exclusive files are the new modules crates/editor-core/src/tools/*.rs,
the four workbench components, the Rust suite and the e2e spec. Four shared
wiring files had to change for those to compile and to satisfy the card's
behavior list; all four were applied locally in this worktree (T21/T09
precedent, integration_files_locally_applied) so the registered acceptance
could actually run. No root manifest / lockfile / router / navigation /
TASKS.json / STATUS.json / package.json / pnpm-workspace.yaml / Cargo.toml /
vitest.config.ts / playwright.config.ts change exists: `pnpm test:task T12`
already resolves through TASKS.json to
`cargo test -p editor-core --test t12_tools --locked` untouched. Cargo.lock is
unchanged (no dependency was added anywhere).

1. crates/editor-core/src/tools.rs — the new-module declaration (the
   testing-contracts.md section 5 "new module declarations go to
   integration.patch" case): `mod dense; mod gesture;` plus the old
   `PointerGesture` helper struct moved into tools/gesture.rs as the
   machine-internal ActiveGesture (it was `pub(crate)` and nothing outside
   editor.rs used it). The public tools exports (Tool, PointerPhase,
   PointerInput, Preview) are byte-identical to before.

2. crates/editor-core/src/editor.rs — delegation into the T12 gesture machine:
   `pointer()` keeps the exact C3 validation/transform and now routes the
   event through tools::gesture::GestureMachine; `finish_pointer`/
   `refresh_preview`/`cancel_gesture` moved into the machine. Two additive
   pieces of crate-internal plumbing: `commit_document_edit` (one history
   entry for an atomic multi-object edit, the "one pointerup = one undo entry"
   unit) and `Editor::viewport()` (read-only, mirroring the T09 get_viewport
   precedent) so the wasm facade can mirror the pan tool's view change. No
   public behavior of Editor changed except the documented T12 semantics:
   Select-tool drags starting on an object move it, handle drags resize it,
   and plain clicks cycle dense stacks (tasks/T12.md required behavior).
   Draw clamp detail: the raw drag must reach 2 CSS px per side before clipping; after clipping
   to canonical image bounds, either side below 2 CSS px (or zero area) rejects the draw. The
   result is not expanded back to the minimum size.

3. crates/wasm-bridge/src/facade.rs — three small fixes the T12 cancel/pan
   semantics require: set_tool and set_viewport refresh the preview overlay
   (a tool/viewport switch cancels the in-flight gesture; the overlay must
   disappear with it), and absorb() mirrors the editor-owned view after every
   delta (the pan tool mutates the editor viewport; without the mirror,
   get_viewport and the renderer would show a stale view — a pre-existing
   T04/T09 divergence the real e2e caught).

4. apps/web/src/lib/editor/EditorHost.ts — the canvas interaction policy the
   card asks to define precisely: pointer capture pairing (set on primary
   pointerdown, released on up/cancel and on every external cancel path),
   cancelGesture() (the Esc/blur/tool-switch/asset-switch seam), window-blur
   cancel, scroll-zoom at the cursor (exp(-pixels*0.002), cancels an active
   gesture), and the contextmenu policy (suppressed on the canvas on every
   platform; never selects/edits/starts gestures). All listeners pair in
   mount/dispose exactly like the T09 set (T09's pairing test stays green) and
   getViewport() passes the additive C3 read-back through.

5. Narrow acceptance after integration (exactly the TASKS.json entry):

       pnpm test:task T12

   Full registered battery (see reports/T12/tests.log for exit codes):

       cargo test --workspace --locked
       cargo fmt --all -- --check
       pnpm exec vitest run
       pnpm --filter @weblabel/web typecheck
       pnpm test:contracts
       REQUIRE_WGPU_DEVICE=1 REQUIRE_HARDWARE_GPU=1 pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/t12_tools.spec.ts --reporter=list

   The e2e builds crates/wasm-bridge via wasm-bindgen itself (pinned toolchain,
   neutral cargo cwd) and needs no playwright.config.ts change: it launches
   full Chromium through file-level test.use({ channel: 'chromium' }).

6. Nothing else is claimed: the save request transport in the e2e is a fetch
   stand-in for the T13 SaveQueue.enqueue wiring; T12 owns only the trigger
   gate (SelectionStore.subscribeSaveNeeded fires for document_changed deltas
   exclusively).

